    "created_at": "2018-01-29T22:53:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-29T22:53:39Z",
    "body": "In the past browsers seem to have preferred to use magic to do this kind of layout instead of using the UA stylesheet. (The difference is observable via getComputedStyle, plus potentially more depending on !important or not.) I'd love to use the UA stylesheet for this and other related issues, but would want to ensure implementers are on board. E.g. the blink-dev thread about the new legacy layout thing notes that Blink is not actually updating its UA styles. Hopefully some of them are watching and can chime in :).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
