    "created_at": "2018-01-29T22:54:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-29T22:56:44Z",
    "body": "If they're not updating the UA styles, then there's no point in having this feature and we should remove it from CSS. :) Its sole purpose for existing is to implement the `align` attribute, it's otherwise a very weird thing to have in CSS...\r\n\r\n“It exists to implement the legacy alignment behavior of HTML’s `<center>` element and `align` attribute.” -- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-align/#justify-items-property",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/361415403/reactions",
